Pattern design and mathematics
  Christopher Carlson, "Multi-Scale Truchet Patterns", Bridges 2018.
  https://christophercarlson.com/portfolio/multi-scale-truchet-patterns/

  This project is an independent reimplementation of those ideas in JavaScript
  (and, for testing, in Python).  It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or
  derived from Carlson's code: no line of his Wolfram Language source was
  translated into this engine.  The engine reproduces the same geometry —
  connection points, circuit tracing, arcs through tangent neighbours, wing
  polygons, depth-parity inversion — because that geometry is what makes the
  patterns behave correctly.

